  "notes": "Portal semantics followed where the Rust impl diverged: NO3 is computed per replicate letter (A/B/C) with calcMinus, so a null NOx or NO2 replicate yields an NA NO3 for that letter and the NO3 mean/sd run na.rm over the remaining pairs (cases no2_null_replicate_* and nox_null_replicate_*). The Rust toolbox pairs positionally over min(len) and its request type (Vec<f64>) cannot represent null replicates at all. NO3 detection accepts both bare and NUT_-prefixed NOx/NO2 species names (case-insensitive on the stripped base); the emitted key is always NUT_NO3_avg/_sd, matching the portal columns. All-NA mean/sd is the portal's KEEP OLD, emitted as an absent key. No constants or curves are used."
